change:
  id: CHG-011
  title: Add the SAAA-owned interactive harness runtime
  status: proposed
  intent: Provide a bounded `saaa sa` session client that exposes SAAA-owned capabilities, target selection and explicit proposer routing before dispatching governed evolution work.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - SYS-001
    - ARCH-001
    - ADR-0003
    - Q-010
    - Q-011
    - RISK-001

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: interactive-harness-session
    requirement: The CLI starts an SAAA-owned session with a deterministic lifecycle and an inspectable capability, skill and route catalog.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: an operator starts `saaa sa` and asks for status, capabilities or skills
        then: the active session, supported target kinds, available skills and registered proposer profiles are reported without invoking an agent
      - id: S2
        when: an operator selects a known route and an explicit target kind and folder
        then: the active session status records that selection and rejects an unknown route without changing the current route
      - id: S3
        when: an operator closes the session
        then: the runtime enters CLOSED and later mutating commands are rejected
  - op: ADDED
    capability: governed-session-evolution
    requirement: The interactive session dispatches only an approved harness-workflow target through the existing deterministic evolution loop.
    scenarios:
      - id: S4
        when: an operator selects a HARNESS_WORKFLOW target and invokes evolve with a declared behaviour case
        then: the selected profile is passed to the existing loop and the session reports its deterministic decision without granting the agent approval authority
      - id: S5
        when: an operator selects a CODE target and invokes evolve with a declared behaviour case
        then: the same deterministic loop evaluates the bounded whole-file change while the session reports CODE as the explicit target kind

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/SaCommandAcceptanceTest.startsAnInspectableSessionWithoutInvokingAnAgent
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: cli/SaCommandAcceptanceTest.recordsExplicitTargetAndRouteAndPreservesRouteAfterInvalidSelection
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: deterministic/HarnessSessionStateMachineTest.rejectsCommandsAfterClose
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: cli/SaCommandAcceptanceTest.evolvesTheSelectedHarnessWorkflowThroughTheExistingLoop
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: cli/SaCommandAcceptanceTest.passesTheExplicitlySelectedRouteRatherThanTheSessionDefaultToTheLoop
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: cli/SaCommandAcceptanceTest.evolvesTheSelectedCodeTargetThroughTheExistingLoop
    layer: acceptance

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add a provider-free session state machine and target vocabulary with unit tests
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add the failing CLI acceptance coverage for catalog, route/target selection and closure
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: implement `saaa sa` line protocol and route harness-workflow execution through EvolveRunner
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: prove code and harness-workflow targets use the same bounded whole-file path, then document the code-realization boundary
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: reconcile active follow-ups, documentation and handoff evidence
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - replacing MCP as the agent-host integration surface
  - automatic model routing based on complexity, budget or ethics
  - a standalone generic sa binary
  - AST-aware or language-specific code mutation
  - a networked or durable multi-process session runtime

risks:
  - RISK-001: an interactive agent experience could be mistaken for an approval authority; only the existing deterministic loop decides
  - Q-010 and Q-011 remain open because exposing explicit route choices is not automatic routing policy
  - whole-file code realization is intentionally partial and needs a later policy before AST or language-aware mutation is introduced
